[38;5;246m  ⎿  · How should other pages and forms load the session module? → ES modules (Recommended)[39m

[38;5;231m⏺[39m ES modules it is. Here's the first section of the design.

  [1mSection 1: Parts and how they connect[0m

  - [1mNew [38;5;153msession.js[0m (at the project root, next to [38;5;153mapp.js[39m): the only code that touches [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m. It provides:
    - [38;5;153msetCurrentUser(userId)[39m: saves the ID under one storage key, e.g. [38;5;153m"currentUserId"[39m.
    - [38;5;153mgetCurrentUserId()[39m: returns the saved ID, or [38;5;153mnull[39m if nobody is logged in.
    - [38;5;153mclearCurrentUser()[39m: removes it. This is logout, as a function only; no logout button until a page needs one.

    Other forms do [38;5;153mimport { getCurrentUserId } from './session.js'[39m and never read storage themselves. That's what lets
    you switch to a cookie later by editing one file.
  - [1m[38;5;153mlogin(username, password)[39m in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m:[0m same signature. It returns [38;5;153m{ success, user, userId }[39m, with [38;5;153muserId = username[39m as
    a clearly marked placeholder until the real API supplies an ID. [38;5;153mlogin[39m itself doesn't touch storage, so it stays
    easy to test.
  - [1mThe form submit handler in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m:[0m after a successful login, calls [38;5;153msetCurrentUser(result.userId)[39m. Saving happens
    here, not inside [38;5;153mlogin[39m.
  - [1m[38;5;153mindex.html[39m:[0m changes [38;5;153m<script src="app.js">[39m to [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m.

  [1mHow it flows:[0m the form is submitted → the input is checked → [38;5;153mlogin()[39m returns [38;5;153m{ …, userId }[39m → the handler calls
  [38;5;153msetCurrentUser(userId)[39m → any later page calls [38;5;153mgetCurrentUserId()[39m.

  [1mLeft out on purpose:[0m a logout button, login expiry, and sending login events to a server. Each is easy to add later
  behind [38;5;153msession.js[39m.

  Does this section look right? Once you confirm, I'll cover error handling and testing.

